# Goertzel ear test
# A manual test, and the instrument is your own ears. Nothing on the installation moves,
# lights or sounds - all of this happens at a desk, with one Mega, a microphone on A0 and
# this computer's own speakers.
# The tone comes out of the computer. The board only samples. The arithmetic - one
# Goertzel bin per frequency - runs here, over the samples as they arrive.
# Sketch: Source code/Arduino/microphone_sampler/. Wiring: hardware setup, "Hearing a tone
# without an MSGEQ7" - two connections, A0 and a ground.
# It never ends on its own - press stop when you are done.

0 Nothing on the piece moves, lights or sounds. No servo is commanded, no NeoPixel changes, no body sings. If the installation is running at all, this run does not touch it.
0 The chosen lead is opened and the board reboots, as an Arduino does whenever a port opens. It greets on the way up with its firmware, the pin it samples and the sample rate it timed for itself, and the page shows that sentence verbatim. If nothing greets, the run stops and says so rather than reading a port with nothing on it.
0.25 Four times a second, from here on: one line to the board, one block of 512 samples back. The board captures at about 19 thousand samples a second, which is a window of 27 milliseconds, and sends the numbers themselves - not a verdict.
0 Every block is measured at all five of the installation's pitches at once - 160, 400, 1000, 2500 and 6250 Hz. That is five passes over 512 numbers, so the five readings are of the same instant, which is the only way to say that one bin rose and the room did not.
0 While nothing is playing, each block sets the floor: what that frequency reads with the room as it is. The page shows the live level and the floor beside it, per pitch, and a `signal span` - if that is zero there is nothing on the pin, and if it is pinned near 1023 the input is clipping.
0 Now press a pitch. A sine of that frequency starts out of this computer's speakers and keeps sounding until you stop it. It is a whole number of cycles long and repeats seamlessly, so there is no click - a click is broadband and would lift every bin at once.
0.4 Nothing is scored for the first four tenths of a second. The sound has to be in the room and the microphone's automatic gain has to stop moving; a floor or a rise taken while the tone is fading up has the tone in it.
0 Then that pitch's row starts showing a rise - its level above its own floor - and the best rise seen since the tone started is kept. Above four, it is called heard.
0 **Listen while it plays.** This is the whole reason a person has to be here. The tone crosses a room, and whether it was ever in the room is not something the software can know - a muted output, an output on the wrong device, a volume at nothing, all read exactly like a microphone that cannot hear. If you cannot hear it either, the fault is on this side and no reading below means anything.
0 Press `silence` when you have listened. The floors are taken again from the next block, so the next pitch is measured against the room as it is now rather than as it was.
0 Walk the five pitches in whatever order you like. A pitch nobody has played is left saying "not played yet" rather than being counted as a failure, and the outcome line names only the ones actually tried.
0 If a rise comes at one pitch and not at another, that is worth more than either alone: the microphone, the lead and the board are plainly working, and what has failed is at that frequency. Low ones failing usually means the microphone module's own high-pass; high ones failing usually means the room, or the speakers.
0 `forget the floors` throws away every floor and every best rise and starts again. Press it after anything that changes the room - a window shut, a fan off, the microphone moved, the volume changed.
0 Nothing is written to a file. Half of this measurement is a sound in the air that no file can hold, and a record of the bins alone would be a record of the half that was never in doubt.
0 Nothing is put back when you stop, because nothing was changed - except that the tone is silenced and the port is closed. The installation is exactly as it was.
